# Sign text: setsign writes through World::set_sign_text, assert_sign
# reads the per-chunk record back. Standing sign at (4,1,8) faces +z at
# rotation 0 — camera on the +z side looks back at its front. The wall
# sign hangs on the +z face of a stone column, same viewing side.
wait_idle 20 6000
debug 0
imgui 0
setblock 4 1 8 STANDING_SIGN 0
setblock 8 1 8 STANDING_SIGN 2
setblock 12 1 8 STONE 0
setblock 12 2 8 STONE 0
setblock 12 1 9 WALL_SIGN 0
wait 30
assert_block 4 1 8 STANDING_SIGN
assert_block 12 1 9 WALL_SIGN
setsign 4 1 8 HELLO WORLD|LINE TWO|line three|LAST LINE
setsign 8 1 8 ROTATED
setsign 12 1 9 WALL SIDE|MOUNTED
assert_sign 4 1 8 HELLO WORLD|LINE TWO|line three|LAST LINE
assert_sign 8 1 8 ROTATED
assert_sign 12 1 9 WALL SIDE|MOUNTED
wait 30
# Front view from +z looking -z (yaw 0): sign at x=4 faces the camera,
# x=8 is rotated 180 so its front is hidden, the wall sign reads on the
# column's +z face.
camera 8 2.2 13.5 0 -2
wait 20
screenshot signs_front
# Close-up of the standing sign's front: lines are centered on the board.
camera 4.5 1.9 11.5 8 -2
wait 20
screenshot sign_close
# Close-up of the wall sign on the column's +z face.
camera 12.5 1.7 12.5 20 -2
wait 20
screenshot wall_close
# The editor path headlessly: signopen -> type/signkey -> signclose
# commits through the same code the real keyboard drives. The camera is
# pinned close enough that the reach check doesn't cancel the edit.
setblock 14 1 9 STANDING_SIGN 0
wait 10
signopen 14 1 9
type FIRST
wait 1
signkey enter
wait 1
type SECOND LINE
wait 5
screenshot sign_editor
signclose
assert_sign 14 1 9 FIRST|SECOND LINE
# Erase path: all-empty text removes the record.
setsign 8 1 8
assert_sign 8 1 8
# Breaking the sign clears its stored text.
setblock 4 1 8 AIR 0
wait 30
assert_block 4 1 8 AIR
assert_sign 4 1 8
echo sign_text done
